          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of
            %em weak model categories
            is a relaxation of that of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semimodel+categories"} semimodel categories
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
          %p
            The weak analogue of the construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy category of a model category
            still exists, as do notions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          %p
            Also, for example, an analogue of left or right
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of model categories
            still makes sense for weak model categories; and, as a bonus in contrast to the usual case, it does not require the assumption of left or right
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} properness
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong weak model category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/premodel+category"} premodel category
            that satisfies the following two
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %strong> Cylinder axiom
                \: Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration"} cofibration
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to X
                from a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant object
                to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant object
                admits a
                %strong relative strong cylinder object
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊔
                        %mi A
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi A
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\sqcup_A X\to I_A X\to X,
              %p
                where the left map is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration"} cofibration
                and its first component
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi A
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to I_A X
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibration"} acyclic cofibration
            %li
              %p
                %strong> Path object axiom
                \: Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to X
                from a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant object
                to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant object
                admits a
                %strong relative strong path object
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi X
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to P_X A\to A\times_X A,
              %p
                where the right map is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
                and its first component
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi X
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_X A\to A
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibration"} acyclic fibration
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_premodel_categories Relation to premodel categories
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/premodel+category"} premodel category
            can be upgraded to a weak model category as follows.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              If a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/premodel+category"} premodel category
              admits a weak Quillen cylinder, then it is a weak model category.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong weak Quillen cylinder
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/premodel+category"} premodel category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint+functors"} left adjoint functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I,D\colon C\to C
              together with the following commutative square of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to C
              %svg{:height => "98.911pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 131.41 98.911", :width => "131.41pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
                %defs
                  %g
                    %symbol{:id => "BNgSSeJbyxJEmM8gx-tQ5YZ85o0=-glyph0-0", :overflow => "visible"}
