              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
              is the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiagonal"} codiagonal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration"} cofibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+cofibration"} trivial cofibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+cofibration"} trivial cofibration
          %p
            Here a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda\colon F\to G
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to C
            is a cofibration if for any (trivial) cofibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to Y
            the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(Y)\sqcup_{F(X)}G(X)\to G(Y)
            is a (trivial) cofibration. Likewise,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            is a trivial cofibration if for any cofibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to Y
            the above map is a trivial cofibration.
          %p
            Reference:
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Henry20"} Henry 20, Section 6
          %p
            This is essentially a reformulation of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structure"} Cisinski–Olschok theory
          %h3#relation_to_model_categories Relation to model categories
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} Model categories
            can be singled out from weak model categories
          %p by adding the following properties:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant object
                admits a strong path object and every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant object
                admits a strong
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
            %li
              %p
                All
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibrations"} acyclic cofibrations
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+cofibrations"} trivial cofibrations
                and all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibrations"} acyclic fibrations
                are
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+fibrations"} trivial fibrations
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/premodel+category"} premodel category
            %li
              %p
                The two classes of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
                corresponding to the left and right induced
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semimodel+structures"} semimodel structures
                coincide.
          %h3#relation_to_combinatorial_model_categories Relation to combinatorial model categories
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial"} combinatorial
            weak model category can be connected to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
            by a zigzag of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          #WeakModelStructureOnSemiSimplicialSets.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+model+structure+on+semi-simplicial+sets"}> weak model structure on semi-simplicial sets
                )
              %br/
              There is a weak model structure on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-simplicial+sets"} semi-simplicial sets
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalen
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} that on simplicial sets
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Henry18"} Henry 18, Thm. 5.5.6
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/premodel+category"} premodel category
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Henry18
              %p
